      "status": "done",
      "seconds": 26,
      "outputType": "markdown",
      "output": "# Beat Studio: Product Spec\n\n## Song format\n- **Song**: name; bpm (60–180); swing (0–0.5, delays each odd 16th by swing × one 16th); key (\"root major/minor\", such as \"A minor\"); patterns A–D; chain (1–16 names from A–D, looped in song mode); mixer.\n- **Pattern**: one bar of 16 sixteenth steps (0–15).\n  - **drums**: kick, snare, clap, chh, ohh, tom, rim and crash, each exactly 16 characters. \".\" is a rest. 1, 2 and 3 are soft, medium and hard, at gain 0.4, 0.7 and 1.0.\n  - **bass**: step, note (MIDI 36–59), len (1–16 steps), accent (true/false) and slide (true/false). The bass is monophonic and notes never overlap. A slide glides into the next note.\n  - **chords**: step, notes (three MIDI notes) and len (1–16 steps). Chords do not overlap.\n- **Mixer**:\n  - drums, bass, keys and fx each have vol (0–1), pan (−1–1) and send (0–1).\n  - master has vol (0–1) and cutoff (200–20000 Hz).\n- Mute and solo are session state and are not saved.\n\n## Layout\n| Zone | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| Transport bar (top) | Play/Stop, Pattern/Song toggle, bpm, swing knob, key, demo menu (House, Lo-fi, Techno) |\n| Row 2 | Pattern bank (A–D, Copy, Clear); drum grid (8 rows × 16 steps, with M and S per row) |\n| Row 3 | Bass piano roll (24 rows, 16 columns, with A and S toggles); chord lane |\n| Bottom | Mixer (4 strips plus master); spectrum visualizer |\n\n- At widths under 720 px, the sections stack in the order above and the page scrolls vertically.\n\n## Interactions\n- **Step click**: toggles a rest to velocity 2, or any velocity to a rest.\n- **Step velocity**: drag up or down by 12 px per level, or long-press (500 ms) to cycle 1→2→3. The step's brightness shows its velocity.\n- **Piano roll**:\n  - Click an empty cell to place a one-step note, replacing any note it overlaps.\n  - Drag a note's right edge to set len.\n  - Click a note to select it; click it again to delete it.\n- **Accent and slide**: the A and S toggles apply to the selected note.\n- **Chord picker**: click a lane step to open I, IV, V and vi triads of the key, plus None. Drag a chord's end to set len.\n- **Pattern bank**:\n  - Click a slot to select it.\n  - Copy, then click a slot, to duplicate the pattern.\n  - Clear empties the current pattern.\n  - In Song mode, click slots to append them to the chain; × removes the last entry.\n- **Knobs**: vertical drag (150 px spans the full range), mouse wheel, or double-click to reset to default.\n- **Faders**: vertical drag; double-click resets to 0.8.\n- **Audio start**: the first Play click unlocks audio. Mouse and touch behave identically.\n\n## Keyboard\n| Key | Action |\n|---|---|\n| Space | Play/Stop |\n| 1–4 | Select pattern A–D |\n| Z X C V B N M | Play bass scale degrees 1–7 of the key, live |\n| Shift + those keys | Same notes, one octave up |\n| A / S | Toggle accent / slide on the selected note |\n| Delete | Remove the selected note |\n\n## Visual style\n| Role | Colour |\n|---|---|\n| Background, graphite | #0f1115 |\n| Panels (frosted glass, 12 px blur) | #171a21 |\n| Primary accent: steps, play, meters | lime #a3e635 |\n| Secondary accent: bass, keys, visualizer | cyan #22d3ee |\n| Text | #e5e7eb |\n\n- **Type**: offline system sans stack (Inter, system-ui, Segoe UI). Body 13 px, labels 11 px uppercase, readouts in tabular monospace.\n\n## Drum voices\n- **Kick**: sine pitch drop from 150 to 50 Hz, warm thump.\n- **Snare**: tone plus band-passed noise, crisp crack.\n- **Clap**: three noise bursts, wide smack.\n- **Closed hat (chh)**: short high-passed noise tick.\n- **Open hat (ohh)**: longer sizzle, choked by chh.\n- **Tom**: pitched sine drop, round knock.\n- **Rim**: short square click, woody.\n- **Crash**: long, bright metallic noise wash.\n\n**Unverified**: this is a specification only. No build, audio playback or timing has been tested."
