      "output": "## Review record — static source review, not actually run\n\nThe page was not opened, no audio was produced and timing was not measured. Every finding below comes from reading the code only.\n\n**Confirmed in source**\n- **Song format:** the demo parser yields drum strings, bass objects (`step`, `note`, `len`, `accent`, `slide`), chords and a mixer. Velocities map to `[.4,.7,1]`.\n- **Scheduling and audio start:** a 25 ms `setInterval` schedules ahead on `ctx.currentTime+0.12`. Swing uses `nt+(st%2?sw*len():0)`. `new AC()` runs only inside `init()`, which is called from Play, Space or the bass keys.\n- **Sound:** all 8 drum voices are present, and the open hat is choked by the closed hat. Bass accent raises gain and filter peak, and slide glides through `setTargetAtTime`. The chord picker offers degrees I/IV/V/vi.\n- **Editing:** patterns A–D, Copy, Clear and song chaining are present. Pointer events with `touch-action:none` cover touch.\n- **Mixer and output:** faders, pan and send controls exist, with RMS meters, a log-scale master filter (200 Hz–20 kHz) and a 64-bar spectrum.\n- **Network:** there are no external requests or libraries.\n\n**Defects**\n1. **No fx mixer strip.** The deck only builds `S=['drums','bass','keys','master']`, although the spec asks for four strips including fx.\n2. **Wrong demo shown in the menu.** The match `['hou','lo','tec'].findIndex(...)` finds \"hou\" inside \"Warehouse Techno\", so loading Techno displays House.\n3. **The S key does two things.** The host map `B={KeyS:0,...}` plays a bass note, while the editor's `if(k==\"s\")tg(\"slide\")` toggles slide. Pressing S triggers both.\n4. **Song mode cannot be edited properly.**\n   - There is no × button to remove the last chain entry, and the chain is not displayed.\n   - `onPattern` pushes to the chain on every slot click, so you cannot view a pattern without appending it.\n5. **Kick pitch is off-spec.** The code sweeps `150→45 Hz` (`exponentialRampToValueAtTime(45,...)`); the spec says 50 Hz.\n6. **Key cannot be changed.** It is a readout only (`kv.textContent`); the spec puts a key control in the transport bar.\n7. **Live bass playing disturbs the sequence.** `g.cancelScheduledValues(t)` can cancel sequenced bass events already in the lookahead window. The `slid` state also carries over between sequenced and live notes.\n8. **Pattern changes reset the editor.** In song mode, every pattern change calls `ed.render`, which destroys any drag in progress.\n\n**Unverified**\n- Whether audio actually sounds and whether timing drifts.\n- Swing as heard.\n- Meter and spectrum motion.\n- Touch and long-press on real devices.\n- The stacked layout under 720 px.\n- The glass blur look.\n- Whether the modules and wiring match the delivered originals: the separate module outputs were not supplied for comparison. The internal APIs are consistent with each other."
